    @* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       #973 L2 · HARLAN FESS, NEBULA MUTUAL. The salesman has crossed the floor and is standing at the
       table — he is not sitting, because he was not invited, and there is no eighth way to open a sitting
       in this codebase. Everything he says comes out of Core (NebulaRep): the tier line, the buttons and
       their prices, his answer to the captain's own line. Nothing here is typed twice.

       AND THE PAGE THAT COMES BACK IS NOT DRAWN HERE. #973 L1 shipped StoryBeats.Beat.Flashback as a
       PLATE — one bleached painting for every memory, riding the edge for its seven seconds over a surface
       that stays readable — and a merged guard pins that presentation. So "I already have a policy" raises
       the beat through the one seam and the seam puts the plate up; this panel draws his pitch and his
       answer and nothing of the plate, because drawing it here as well would be the stacked card #777 named
       (the same picture, twice, on one screen).
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ *@
    @if (_repCard is { } pitch)
    {
        <RepCard _repSaid="@_repSaid" AnswerTheRep="@AnswerTheRep" CloseTheRepsCard="@CloseTheRepsCard"
                 Dismiss="@Dismiss" pitch="@pitch" />
