    @* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       #1061 beat 2 · BREM KOLT, HAZARDOUS ACCOUNTS. The same firm as the panel above and deliberately the
       same markup — one .rep-card, one scrim, one shell — because he is a salesman from Nebula Mutual and
       drawing him differently would be the page claiming a difference the fiction does not have.

       WHAT IS DIFFERENT IS TWO THINGS. There is NO PORTRAIT: Fess has the one portrait arc 2 allows, and
       hanging his face over Kolt's name would be the third named bug class with a photograph on it (the
       picture reporting a man the sim is not holding). Caption-only is #528's deliberate no-picture idiom
       and it is taken on purpose here, not by omission — no plate in this repository is a picture of him.
       And his line is TWO sentences, because the canon is two: the opener and the pitch, in that order.

       AND THE WAY OUT IS HIS REFUSAL. A ✕ that only took the panel away would leave a man standing at your
       elbow on open regolith with nothing left to answer — so the dismiss runs the verb "Not today" runs:
       he says the third line, and it is the only thing he has to say about being turned down.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ *@
    @if (_hardcaseCard is { } koltOffers)
    {
